course: dictionary
lesson: 6182
title: A mirage is not really there
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mirage is something you seem to see that is not really there. The sentences around the word give you the clues. «A mirage on a hot road is hot air bending light from the sky, not real water.» The sentence says it is not real water, so a mirage looks real but is not.
explain: A mirage can also be a hope or idea that seems real but is not. Think of a thirsty traveller who sees water ahead and then finds only dry sand. Like the water on the road, the hope was not really there.
explain: Scientists explain why mirages happen. Light bends when it passes through layers of hot and cooler air. «A mirage of water on a hot road is light from the sky bent by hot air near the road, which is why the puddle vanishes as you get closer.» Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: A mirage is something you seem to see that is not really there.
fact: Mirages happen when light bends through layers of hot and cooler air.
fact: On a hot day, the road ahead can look like a pool of water that disappears as you get closer.
fact: A mirage can also be a hope or idea that seems real but is not.
fact: «Mirage» is a noun: a mirage, mirages.
exercise: «A mirage on a hot road is hot air bending light from the sky, not real water.» What is a mirage in this sentence? | A type of cloud | A hot wind | A pool of real water | *Something that seems to be there but is not
exercise: Thirsty travellers in the desert see «water» ahead that disappears as they get closer. What is the «water»? | A storm cloud | A river hidden under the sand | *A mirage | A real lake full of fish
exercise: «A mirage of water on a hot road is light from the sky bent by hot air near the road, which is why the puddle vanishes as you get closer.» Why does the puddle vanish? | Because the rain dried up | *Because the water was never real, only light bent by hot air | Because the road is wet and slippery | Because it was a hole in the road
test: «It was only a mirage.» What does mirage mean here? | A real storm | *Something that looked real but was not | A kind of desert animal | A wet, muddy path
test: Which sentence uses mirage to mean a hope that seems real but is not? | *The sailors clung to the mirage of a rescue ship that never came. | The sun rose early over the hills. | The bridge was built of solid stone. | Her coat was warm and red.
exam: Is a mirage real water? | *No, it is light from the sky bent by hot air | Yes, it is a puddle left by the rain | No, it is a kind of cloud that never moves | Yes, it is a river under the road
